",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/excel-shortcuts-keys\/#faq-question-1741860214458\",\"position\":2,\"url\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/excel-shortcuts-keys\/#faq-question-1741860214458\",\"name\":\"Why should we use Excel shortcut keys?\",\"answerCount\":1,\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Shortcut keys can reduce the time spent on repetitive tasks, which improves efficiency, minimizes mouse clicks, enhances productivity, and allows us to focus on data and analysis. They are especially useful for power users and professionals working with large datasets.\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/excel-shortcuts-keys\/#faq-question-1741860227910\",\"position\":3,\"url\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/excel-shortcuts-keys\/#faq-question-1741860227910\",\"name\":\"What are some essential shortcut keys for editing and entering data in Excel?\",\"answerCount\":1,\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Excel shortcut keys used to edit and enter data are<br\/><strong>F2:<\/strong> Edit the active cell<br\/><strong>Alt+=:<\/strong> Automatically insert an AutoSum formula<br\/><strong>Ctrl+Enter:<\/strong> Fill selected cells with the current entry<br\/><strong>Ctrl+;<\/strong> and <strong>Ctrl+Shift+;:<\/strong> Insert the current date and time, respectively\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/excel-shortcuts-keys\/#faq-question-1741860243758\",\"position\":4,\"url\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/excel-shortcuts-keys\/#faq-question-1741860243758\",\"name\":\"How do shortcut keys help in selecting data in Excel?\",\"answerCount\":1,\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Using shortcut keys to select data enables us to highlight ranges or entire rows\/columns. For example: Shift+Space: Selects the entire row, Ctrl+Shift+Arrow Keys: Extends the selection to the edge of contiguous data, Ctrl+A: Selects the entire worksheet or current data region, and Ctrl+Space: Selects the entire column.\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/excel-shortcuts-keys\/#faq-question-1741860260111\",\"position\":5,\"url\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/excel-shortcuts-keys\/#faq-question-1741860260111\",\"name\":\"How can I learn and remember all shortcut keys?\",\"answerCount\":1,\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Create a cheat sheet and keep it near your workstation, practice regularly using one new shortcut per day, enrol in online tutorials and interactive guides to reinforce memory, and customize your own quick-reference guide.\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/excel-shortcuts-keys\/#faq-question-1741860273731\",\"position\":6,\"url\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/excel-shortcuts-keys\/#faq-question-1741860273731\",\"name\":\"Are Excel shortcut keys the same on all operating systems?\",\"answerCount\":1,\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Although most shortcut keys are similar between Windows and Mac versions of Excel, there are some differences in key combinations. For instance, the Command key on Mac often replaces the Ctrl key found on Windows.\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/excel-shortcuts-keys\/#faq-question-1741860285147\",\"position\":7,\"url\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/excel-shortcuts-keys\/#faq-question-1741860285147\",\"name\":\"Can I customize Excel shortcut keys?\",\"answerCount\":1,\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Excel doesn\u2019t have a feature to allow full customization of all shortcut keys, but by using VBA (Visual Basic for Applications), you can create macros that can be assigned custom shortcuts, or third-party add-ins may provide additional customization options.\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/excel-shortcuts-keys\/#faq-question-1741860299564\",\"position\":8,\"url\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/excel-shortcuts-keys\/#faq-question-1741860299564\",\"name\":\"How do I format cells quickly using shortcut keys?\",\"answerCount\":1,\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Excel shortcut keys to format cells are F2 to edit a cell, Ctrl + Shift + _ to remove the outline border of the cells, Alt + H + H to fill colors, Ctrl + Shift + &amp; to add an outline to the select cells, Shift + Tab to move to the previous cell, and Ctrl + I, Ctrl + B to italicize and bold the font.\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/excel-shortcuts-keys\/#faq-question-1741860312710\",\"position\":9,\"url\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/excel-shortcuts-keys\/#faq-question-1741860312710\",\"name\":\"How can I quickly copy, cut, and paste cells using shortcuts?\",\"answerCount\":1,\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Use Ctrl+C for copy, Ctrl+X for cut, and Ctrl+V for paste. You can also use advanced options, such as Ctrl+Alt+V to open the Paste Special dialog, which allows you to paste specific elements like values, formulas, or formatting.\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/excel-shortcuts-keys\/#faq-question-1741860326043\",\"position\":10,\"url\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/excel-shortcuts-keys\/#faq-question-1741860326043\",\"name\":\"\u00a0Is it possible to quickly switch between multiple worksheets using keyboard shortcuts?\",\"answerCount\":1,\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"You can switch between several sheets by using Ctrl+Page Up to move to the previous worksheet and Ctrl+Page Down to move to the next worksheet.\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/excel-shortcuts-keys\/#faq-question-1741860339179\",\"position\":11,\"url\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/excel-shortcuts-keys\/#faq-question-1741860339179\",\"name\":\"How do I quickly open or save a workbook using shortcuts?\",\"answerCount\":1,\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"We can open a workbook using Ctrl+O and save the current file using Ctrl+S. Additionally, F12 lets us open the Save As dialog to save under a new name or location.\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"}]}<\/script>\n<!-- \/ Yoast SEO plugin. -->","yoast_head_json":{"title":"100+ MS Excel Shortcut Keys You Must Know in 2026","description":"Master Excel like a pro with our comprehensive list of the top 70 keyboard shortcuts for Excel in 2026. Boost your productivity and efficiency. Read now!","robots":{"index":"index","follow":"follow","max-snippet":"max-snippet:-1","max-image-preview":"max-image-preview:large","max-video-preview":"max-video-preview:-1"},"canonical":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/excel-shortcuts-keys\/","og_locale":"en_US","og_type":"article","og_title":"100+ MS Excel Shortcut Keys You Must Know in 2026","og_description":"Master Excel like a pro with our comprehensive list of the top 70 keyboard shortcuts for Excel in 2026. Boost your productivity and efficiency. Read now!","og_url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/excel-shortcuts-keys\/","og_site_name":"WsCube Tech Blog","article_publisher":"https:\/\/www.facebook.com\/wscubetech.india","article_published_time":"2025-03-13T10:16:13+00:00","article_modified_time":"2026-08-03T10:40:11+00:00","og_image":[{"width":1654,"height":800,"url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/03\/ms-excel-shortcut-keys.webp","